# Real Git process boundary control

The existing direct-pipe profile measures the directly created process and
explicitly excludes descendants. Before attributing useful Git CPU to that
counter, establish whether the local launcher is itself the native Git process.
This control answers only that identity question. It does not rerun V6, the
twenty-case helper profile or the 96-call pipe cohort.

The independent diagnostic policy fixes the installed cmd and mingw64 image
paths and SHA256 values before execution. Existing environment/effect preflight
remains active. One `git --no-optional-locks cat-file --batch` receives no object
request. Its retained stdin keeps the native process observable without alias
scripts, source edits, a persistent production reader or configuration changes.

The original Popen process handle is borrowed, not reacquired by PID. The
existing HeldLineage reader requires one exact native-child shape, two matching
process snapshots and full live parent/child identity and creation brackets.
There is one attachment attempt; absence is bounded discovery, not a refused
attempt followed by retry. Both original objects must become terminal after
closing stdin, with root exit zero and empty stdout/stderr. Query-handle cleanup
failure overrides success. A root-only kill fallback is failure handling, not
proof about an unobserved child or all writers.

The new diagnostic has a ten-second run bound from before spawn, a five-second
discovery bound within it, at most 100 discovery snapshots and a separate
five-second cleanup bound. Late attachment/exit/cleanup witnesses refuse. All
existing 300/60/10 admission origins, live observations and 780-second package
guard remain unchanged. No native API or release implementation changes.

The observation proves only this finite control's held cmd-to-native edge.
On-disk before/after hash equality is not mapped-image attestation or an ABA
proof. Full paths, process parent fields and live handles are local diagnostic
evidence, not authenticated production ownership. The control does not observe
every descendant, establish old cohorts' topology, measure creation/copy/wait
cost, accept observer overhead or provide a speedup. Existing old counters retain
their narrower directly-created-process meaning.

Run models first, commit this protocol and implementation, then issue one local
control through the source-preserving wrapper. Retain its first outcome without
retry-to-pass. A refusal means the topology gate is unproven, not permission to
select another process or image. The CLI accepts a bounded fresh label only:

```text
python -m unittest discover -s tools/xtask-package-attribution-074 -p test_git_process_boundary.py
python tools/xtask-package-attribution-074/git_process_boundary.py control first
```

Output is exclusively created under `target/git-process-boundary-20261026`.
There are no server, service, clock, dependency, product-load or qualification
operations. The source helpers and all first failures remain unchanged.
